$DIR/test.p:3:2: len("x") is a call of the built-in function len, which returns no error for or to test
    An or clause tests the error that a function returns as its last result. A
    conversion, such as int64(x), and a call of a built-in function, such as
    len(s), are written like calls, but they call no function and return no
    error, so there is nothing for or to test.
    Remove the or clause, or call a function that returns an error.
    (see "Or clauses" in the Plutonium spec, section 11.27)
    (run "pluto explain E2461" for a longer explanation)
